=== REAL LOGIN redirect_to FLOW (determined empirically from the running servers) ===
1. GET  /user/login?redirect_to=<url-encoded vector>
     -> Gitea sets cookies: redirect_to=<enc>, i_like_gitea (session),
        and (1.16.x only) a _csrf cookie + hidden <input name="_csrf"> in the HTML.
        1.26.0 protects the login form with SameSite-Lax cookies and has NO _csrf field.
2. POST /user/login   user_name=pcbuser & password=pcbpassword123 (+ _csrf on 1.16.x),
        reusing the cookie jar.
     -> successful auth -> handleSignIn -> (*Context).RedirectToFirst(redirect_to cookie)
        -> ctx.Redirect -> Go stdlib http.Redirect -> 302 (1.16.x) / 303 (1.26.0) Location.
   The Location header of this POST is the observable the oracle reads.
control: redirect_to=/explore/repos  ->  Location: /explore/repos on ALL THREE versions,
        proving the POST authenticates and redirect_to is genuinely honored (so a Location:/
        is a real validator block, not a failed login).

